WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Welcome to the video on addressing Amazon's multiple accounts policy

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:04.994
violations.

00:00:04.994 --> 00:00:08.031
This video covers the following topics; 1.

00:00:08.031 --> 00:00:10.200
What can you do to

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.233
address violations?

00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:11.750
2.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.333
Best practices to remain compliant.

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:16.400
The content in this

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.080
video applies to all stores.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.440
Let us first understand how you can respond to a

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.227
violation notice.

00:00:22.227 --> 00:00:26.160
If you receive a notification that a related account has

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.900
been deactivated, this means that one of your existing accounts violated Amazon's

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:31.332
policies.

00:00:31.332 --> 00:00:36.080
In order to reactivate your related account, you must first address

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.440
the violation in the underlying account that was responsible for the policy

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.763
violations by submitting an appeal for each violation.

00:00:43.763 --> 00:00:45.840
You can appeal by signing

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.655
into the account that was responsible for the policy violations.

00:00:49.655 --> 00:00:50.800
You must appeal

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.200
in each regional Amazon store in which the account has been deactivated for the

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:55.980
policy violation.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.880
You can submit your appeal by accessing your account health

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:00.267
dashboard.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:04.140
If your appeal for the underlying account that was responsible

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.920
for the policy violations is accepted and the account is successfully reactivated,

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.340
you can then appeal your related account.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.760
When submitting the appeal, you will need

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.720
to provide us with the storefront name of the original account that was reactivated

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.920
and the date of reactivation.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.680
Use case number one.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.880
You own two selling accounts,

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.492
seller storefront one, and seller storefront two.

00:01:27.492 --> 00:01:29.040
Seller storefront one

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.120
receives a deactivation notice for directing customers to an external site

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.113
circumventing the sales process.

00:01:35.113 --> 00:01:38.600
You then receive a deactivation notice on

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:42.906
seller storefront two since it is related to seller storefront one.

00:01:42.906 --> 00:01:44.080
You should log

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.803
into your seller storefront one account and appeal the violation.

00:01:47.803 --> 00:01:48.920
If your appeal

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.320
is accepted and the seller storefront one account is successfully reactivated,

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.400
then log into your seller storefront two account and appeal through the

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.120
account health dashboard by providing the storefront name of the original

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.720
account that was reactivated and the date of reactivation.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.320
If you believe the

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.600
related account deactivation happened in error or you have never owned or

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:14.720
operated another account, please submit an appeal through the account health

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.651
dashboard and confirm that the account is not related to yours.

00:02:18.651 --> 00:02:20.080
If we do not

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.040
receive evidence confirming the account is not related to you, the account will

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.074
not be reinstated.

00:02:25.074 --> 00:02:28.520
If you previously co-owned or co-operated the underlying

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.960
account with a former business partner, you would need to provide supporting

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:36.440
documentation such as a contract showing separation of the business relationship

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.200
as part of the appeal.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.720
Please note that it's against policy to buy, sell, or

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.577
transfer your account to or from another seller.

00:02:44.577 --> 00:02:46.720
Let us learn about the best

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.347
practices to remain compliant.

00:02:48.347 --> 00:02:51.600
Sellers who have a legitimate business reason for

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.480
operating more than one account and maintain all accounts in good standing

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.988
will not be at risk for a multiple accounts deactivation.

00:02:58.988 --> 00:03:00.040
Please make sure

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.655
you only create additional accounts if there is a valid business reason.

00:03:04.655 --> 00:03:05.040
Examples

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.320
of valid business reasons include owning separate brands with different

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.820
storefront names or selling products manufactured by different companies.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:13.320
When

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.960
you receive notices or see alerts on your account health dashboard or

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.600
performance notifications from Amazon that indicate you are violating Amazon

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.120
selling policies, please correct the behavior and submit an appeal if applicable

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.613
as soon as possible.

00:03:27.613 --> 00:03:30.600
Opening a new account instead of addressing the

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.600
underlying violations within your existing accounts is a violation of

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:39.120
Amazon's policies and will only trigger an automatic deactivation on your

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.151
related accounts.

00:03:40.151 --> 00:03:43.760
All sellers are responsible for understanding and

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.120
adhering to the terms and conditions set out by Amazon's business solutions

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.080
agreement which is part of the registration process and includes the

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.113
selling policies and seller code of conduct.

00:03:55.113 --> 00:03:57.280
All sellers are expected to

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:01.062
maintain and keep secure their own account information and credentials.

00:04:01.062 --> 00:04:01.440
In

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.920
the primary account information, sellers should not list information of any

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.309
third-party services they may be using to help manage the account.

00:04:10.309 --> 00:04:11.040
However, if

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:15.360
you have engaged a valid third-party service, we recommend listing them as a

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.217
secondary user in the approved app Users User Permissions.

00:04:19.217 --> 00:04:21.360
We hope this video on

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.462
our multiple accounts policy was helpful.

00:04:24.462 --> 00:04:27.267
Thank you and happy selling on Amazon!
